lf-contract 0.1
# sha-big-sigma0 is an IR 0.2 word (src/program/sha-words.fs uses LSHIFT
# and -ROT): leanforth verify refuses it, since its receipt needs schema
# 0.4, which awaits the owner's [format] gate (plan 8.4.1k). Contract
# language 0.1 has no bitwise operations either; what the word computes is
# proved by Lean (shaBigSigma0_correct in tests/reference/program-ir.lean)
# and its export re-checked by LeanForth (make reference-program-sha-export).
# This contract states only the range of the result. No expect line: the
# outcome is the refusal, not one of the generator's.
id sha-big-sigma0/0
word sha-big-sigma0
ir tests/program/ir/sha-words.ir
stack ( u -- u' )
inputs u
statement For a 32-bit word u the word returns a 32-bit word (FIPS 180-4's Sigma0(u), which this contract language cannot state).
pre 0 <= u && u <= 4294967295
case true
  out r
  ensure 0 <= r && r <= 4294967295
